			<h2>What is a function?</h2>
	
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>Every block you see in Blockly makes Zumi do a different action. These blocks run code called <strong>functions.</strong> Think of functions as packages of code that you can use to write your programs. Functions can have inputs and outputs. Blocks that require inputs will have a space for you to input some values. These extra pieces of information are called <strong>parameters. </strong>Here are some sample blocks that have parameters:</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="808" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.30.54-AM-1024x808.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="zumi blockly examples with parameters" title="zumi blockly examples with parameters" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.30.54-AM-1024x808.png 1024w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.30.54-AM-300x237.png 300w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.30.54-AM.png 1430w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>
</div>
</div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><a id="6a2214d291f61" name="6a2214d291f61" class="scroll-spy-anchor"></a>
<div class="robolink-step ">

		<div class="robolink-step-head"><span>Step 2</span></div>
	
			<h2>Drive forward</h2>
	
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>It&#8217;s time to make Zumi move! Open the &#8220;Driving&#8221; menu from the Junior blocks tab to see all of the Junior driving functions.</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="835" height="1024" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.38.22-AM-835x1024.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="zumi blockly driving menu" title="zumi blockly driving menu" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.38.22-AM-835x1024.png 835w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.38.22-AM-245x300.png 245w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.38.22-AM.png 1718w" sizes="(max-width: 835px) 100vw, 835px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>

	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>Click and drag the forward block into the workspace and press the green &#8220;Run&#8221; button. Make sure Zumi has enough space!</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="468" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.41.44-AM-1024x468.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="zumi blockly forward block" title="zumi blockly forward block" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.41.44-AM-1024x468.png 1024w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.41.44-AM-300x137.png 300w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.41.44-AM.png 1290w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>

	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>Did Zumi drive forward? Now try changing the seconds <strong>parameter. </strong>Remember that a parameter is an input that can modify a function. Try driving forward for 3 seconds now.</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="257" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.43.08-AM-1024x257.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="zumi blockly forward with 3 seconds" title="zumi blockly forward with 3 seconds" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.43.08-AM-1024x257.png 1024w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.43.08-AM-300x75.png 300w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.43.08-AM.png 1082w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>

	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>You can also change the speed that Zumi drives at! Try changing the speed parameter to 20. Speed always ranges from 0 to 100. No, this is not in miles per hour! It is related to Zumi&#8217;s battery power.</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="257" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.44.22-AM-1024x257.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="zumi blockly drive change speed" title="zumi blockly drive change speed" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.44.22-AM-1024x257.png 1024w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.44.22-AM-300x75.png 300w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.44.22-AM.png 1092w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>
</div>
</div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><a id="6a2214d29386a" name="6a2214d29386a" class="scroll-spy-anchor"></a>
<div class="robolink-step ">

		<div class="robolink-step-head"><span>Step 3</span></div>
	
			<h2>Wait!</h2>
	
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>You can connect more than one forward block in a row. Attach some forward blocks together like this. Feel free to change the parameters!</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="565" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.47.06-AM-1024x565.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="zumi blockly three forwards in a row" title="zumi blockly three forwards in a row" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.47.06-AM-1024x565.png 1024w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.47.06-AM-300x166.png 300w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-11.47.06-AM.png 1116w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>

	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>Right now it&#8217;s hard to tell when one function ends and the next one begins. Sometimes you want to make the program wait between functions. Open the timing menu and find the &#8220;Wait&#8221; block.</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="590" height="1024" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.12.52-PM-590x1024.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="zumi blockly timing menu" title="zumi blockly timing menu" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.12.52-PM-590x1024.png 590w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.12.52-PM-173x300.png 173w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.12.52-PM.png 1216w" sizes="(max-width: 590px) 100vw, 590px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>

	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>Then, add a wait for 1 second in between each drive command. Rerun your code and watch what happens. You can also try changing the seconds parameter in the &#8220;Wait&#8221; blocks to pause for longer between each drive command.</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="809" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.13.54-PM-1024x809.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="zumi blockly forwards with waits" title="zumi blockly forwards with waits" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.13.54-PM-1024x809.png 1024w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.13.54-PM-300x237.png 300w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.13.54-PM.png 1076w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>
</div>
</div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><a id="6a2214d29424a" name="6a2214d29424a" class="scroll-spy-anchor"></a>
<div class="robolink-step ">

		<div class="robolink-step-head"><span>Step 4</span></div>
	
			<h2>Reverse</h2>
	
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>The reverse function works almost exactly the same as the forward function. It has a seconds parameter that you can change to set how long Zumi drives. Let&#8217;s drive forward for 2 seconds, wait for 2 seconds, then drive in reverse for 2 seconds to return to the start.</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="535" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.23.36-PM-1024x535.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="zumi blockly reverse example" title="zumi blockly reverse example" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.23.36-PM-1024x535.png 1024w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.23.36-PM-300x157.png 300w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.23.36-PM.png 1076w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>
</div>
</div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><a id="6a2214d295af4" name="6a2214d295af4" class="scroll-spy-anchor"></a>
<div class="robolink-step ">

		<div class="robolink-step-head"><span>Step 5</span></div>
	
			<h2>Turning</h2>
	
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>Roads have curves, bends, and turns that Zumi should be able to navigate. There are two turn functions that you can use. One block is for right turns and one block is for left turns. For each turn that you want to make, you need to know how many <strong>degrees</strong> you want to turn.</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="176" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.25.54-PM-1024x176.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="zumi blockly turn left and right" title="zumi blockly turn left and right" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.25.54-PM-1024x176.png 1024w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.25.54-PM-300x51.png 300w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.25.54-PM.png 1376w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>

	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>Practice driving and turning! You can try different angles by changing the degrees parameter.</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="581" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.27.41-PM-1024x581.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="zumi blockly driving and turning" title="zumi blockly driving and turning" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.27.41-PM-1024x581.png 1024w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.27.41-PM-300x170.png 300w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.27.41-PM.png 1082w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>

	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>If you need some help figuring out the degrees, remember that a circle has 360 degrees. Use this chart to help you.</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="900" height="360" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/zumi_angle-900x360.jpg" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="zumi turn angles" title="zumi turn angles" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/zumi_angle.jpg 900w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/zumi_angle-300x120.jpg 300w" sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 900px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>
</div>
</div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><a id="6a2214d29660c" name="6a2214d29660c" class="scroll-spy-anchor"></a>
<div class="robolink-step ">

		<div class="robolink-step-head"><span>Step 6</span></div>
	
			<h2>Challenge: Square</h2>
	
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>It&#8217;s time for your first challenge! Using what you know so far, program Zumi to drive in a square around the block. Remember, a square has four sides all the same length and right angle turns. You can use either all right turns or all left turns. If you are stuck, take a look at image below. When you&#8217;re done, scroll down to see the solution.</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="443" height="454" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/square-443x454.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="" title="square" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/square.png 443w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/square-293x300.png 293w" sizes="(max-width: 443px) 100vw, 443px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>
</div>
</div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><a id="6a2214d297060" name="6a2214d297060" class="scroll-spy-anchor"></a>
<div class="robolink-step ">

		<div class="robolink-step-head"><span>Step 7</span></div>
	
			<h2>Solution: Square</h2>
	
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>If you have something similar to the code below, good job! Pop quiz! How would you make the square bigger or smaller?</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="724" height="1024" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.34.48-PM-724x1024.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="zumi blockly square code" title="zumi blockly square code" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.34.48-PM-724x1024.png 724w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.34.48-PM-212x300.png 212w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-07-13-at-12.34.48-PM.png 1074w" sizes="(max-width: 724px) 100vw, 724px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>

	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>To make the square bigger or smaller, you would need to change all of the durations for the forward blocks. There is a way to make this code more efficient, but you will learn about that later.</p>

		</div>
	</div>
</div>
</div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><a id="6a2214d298238" name="6a2214d298238" class="scroll-spy-anchor"></a>
<div class="robolink-step ">

		<div class="robolink-step-head"><span>Step 8</span></div>
	
			<h2>U-turns</h2>
	
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>If Zumi makes a wrong turn, what should she do? In the real world, reversing down the street would not be a good idea. Practice doing a U-turn with the U-turn blocks. There is a new parameter for speed which can be anywhere from 0 to 100. Safe U-turns should be done at low speeds, just like real-life!</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="828" height="517" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/left_u_turn_right_u_turn-828x517.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="" title="left_u_turn_right_u_turn" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/left_u_turn_right_u_turn.png 828w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/left_u_turn_right_u_turn-300x187.png 300w" sizes="(max-width: 828px) 100vw, 828px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>

	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p><strong>Activity: </strong>Build your own &#8220;street&#8221;. You can use paper to draw one or use household objects like pens and pencils to create a lane. Have Zumi drive down the street and make a left U-turn at the end of the street and drive back. Make sure to include a wait before your U-turn to check for oncoming traffic. See below for an example code.</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
