<div class="robolink-step ">

		<div class="robolink-step-head"><span>Step 10</span></div>
	
			<h2>Calibrate the gyroscope</h2>
	
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>A gyroscope is a sensor that helps Zumi drive straight. You will learn about the gyroscope more later, but if you feel like your Zumi is driving a little bit sideways you can use the calibrate gyro block at the beginning of your program.</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="496" height="216" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-06-10-at-12.55.17-PM-496x216.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="zumi blockly calibrate gyro" title="zumi blockly calibrate gyro" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-06-10-at-12.55.17-PM.png 496w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-06-10-at-12.55.17-PM-300x131.png 300w" sizes="(max-width: 496px) 100vw, 496px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>
</div>
</div></div></div></div><div class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-sm-12"><div class="vc_column-inner"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><a id="6a2214d29bc64" name="6a2214d29bc64" class="scroll-spy-anchor"></a>
<div class="robolink-step ">

		<div class="robolink-step-head"><span>Step 11</span></div>
	
			<h2>Shapes and Sequences</h2>
	
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>You learned how to program your own square using drive commands, but you can use some of the shape blocks instead. Open the &#8220;Shapes&#8221; menu to access them. You can change if the shape turns left or right but you will not be able to change the speed or the size. You can do that as a challenge!</p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div  class="wpb_single_image wpb_content_element vc_align_center wpb_content_element">
		
		<figure class="wpb_wrapper vc_figure">
			<div class="vc_single_image-wrapper   vc_box_border_grey"><img decoding="async" width="1024" height="1008" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-06-14-at-11.55.16-AM-1024x1008.png" class="vc_single_image-img attachment-large" alt="zumi blockly shapes menu" title="zumi blockly shapes menu" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-06-14-at-11.55.16-AM-1024x1008.png 1024w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-06-14-at-11.55.16-AM-300x295.png 300w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/Screen-Shot-2021-06-14-at-11.55.16-AM.png 1286w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></div>
		</figure>
	</div>

	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>There are two blocks in this list that you may not be familiar with yet: the figure-8 and J-curve turns. This is what those movements look like:</p>

		</div>
	</div>
<div class="wpb_images_carousel wpb_content_element vc_clearfix wpb_content_element"><div class="wpb_wrapper"><div id="vc_images-carousel-1-1780618450" data-ride="vc_carousel" data-wrap="false" style="width: 1024px;" data-interval="0" data-auto-height="yes" data-mode="horizontal" data-partial="false" data-per-view="2" data-hide-on-end="true" class="vc_slide vc_images_carousel"><ol class="vc_carousel-indicators"><li data-target="#vc_images-carousel-1-1780618450" data-slide-to="0"></li><li data-target="#vc_images-carousel-1-1780618450" data-slide-to="1"></li></ol><div class="vc_carousel-inner"><div class="vc_carousel-slideline"><div class="vc_carousel-slideline-inner"><div class="vc_item"><div class="vc_inner"><a class="" href="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/zumi_figure_8-529x360.jpg" data-lightbox="lightbox[rel-2912-3833646936]"><img decoding="async" width="529" height="360" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/zumi_figure_8-529x360.jpg" class="attachment-large" alt="zumi_figure_8" title="zumi_figure_8" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/zumi_figure_8.jpg 529w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/zumi_figure_8-300x204.jpg 300w" sizes="(max-width: 529px) 100vw, 529px" /></a></div></div><div class="vc_item"><div class="vc_inner"><a class="" href="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/zumi_j_turn-copy-360x675.jpg" data-lightbox="lightbox[rel-2912-3833646936]"><img decoding="async" width="360" height="675" src="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/zumi_j_turn-copy-360x675.jpg" class="attachment-large" alt="zumi_j_turn" title="zumi_j_turn" srcset="https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/zumi_j_turn-copy.jpg 360w, https://archive.learn.robolink.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/zumi_j_turn-copy-160x300.jpg 160w" sizes="(max-width: 360px) 100vw, 360px" /></a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p>Use these blocks when you want to show off your driving skills!</p>

		</div>
	</div>
